  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Qt: Don't apply the old filter when selecting from the completer",
  "description": "If DisplayFilterEdit::applyDisplayFilter() is called when\nthe completer's popup has a valid QModelIndex, then that\nmeans that the DisplayFilterEdit::returnPressed signal is\nbeing handled before QAbstractItemView::activated from the\nQCompleter's popup. Both get triggered by pressing Return or\nEnter. (Clicking an item in the completer sends\nQAbstractItemView::activated but not DisplayFilterEdit::returnPressed.)\n\nIn such a case, the DisplayFilterEdit's text() has the old value,\nnot the value from the completer, and the value hasn't been\nsyntax checked yet. (It probably is valid, but the saved display\nfilter file could have invalid filters due to changes between\nversions, fields from UATs, fields from removed columns, etc.)\n\nDon't filter the packets with the old filter, even if the value\nwas valid; only let the completer set the LineEdit's text.\nActually applying the filter will require pressing Enter a\nsecond time, just as if the old filter were invalid or if the\ncompleter item had been chosen via clicking instead.\n\nFix #19323",
